caption: Authority and Core Principles
rule: authority-and-core-principles

This document is the current GATES authority for Drives, Drive Marks, source changes, and Mark-to-character-point conversion. Campaign rulings configure the options identified here but should not silently change the end-of-session procedure.

A Drive rewards a player for expressing an important part of a player character, campaign, or setting through play. Drives are deliberate behavioral incentives. They are not compulsory behavior, objective morality, or substitutes for Oaths, Codes of Honor, Vows, Duties, and other mandatory mechanics.

This is a player-character-facing system. A player character's active sources and secondary choices cannot be replaced involuntarily. External events may destroy a nation, kill a god, expel the character, remove abilities, alter memories, or make a Drive difficult to fulfill, but they do not rewrite the character's Drive identity without the player's voluntary choice.

A source does not need to be objectively true, currently existing, historically accurate, or recognized by outsiders. A lost, adopted, reconstructed, mythologized, or wholly mistaken identity may qualify whenever the campaign permits it and the player selects it.

Points per Mark, starting character value, and Prestige reset value are campaign-level decisions.
